     [38;5;246mIn-memory ring buffer, retrievable on demand. No network, no dependency. Sink stays swappable for a POST later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Console only, structured
     [38;5;246mLeveled, structured console output. Cheapest possible; you only see logs if someone sends them to you.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m POST to our own endpoint
     [38;5;246mShip batches to a collector we run. Real unattended visibility, but the endpoint doesn't exist yet and redaction [39m
     [38;5;246mbecomes a blocker.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Third-party service
     [38;5;246mSentry or similar. Buys the collector and UI; costs a dependency, an account, and sending login-flow data to a [39m
